functions.description:
Answers workplace analytics questions (reservations, occupancy, check-in rate, missed check-ins, room hours, workplace requests filed or resolved, time to resolve) over a period, optionally broken down by up to two dimensions and filtered. Measures, dimensions and member IDs are listed in the Reports section of your instructions; if that section is missing, tell the user reports are not enabled for them. Returns the total, the top rows and a short series; then reply with response_type report_result carrying the same query. Examples:
- "How busy were the desks last month?" -> {"measure": "occupancy", "filters": [{"dimension": "resource_type", "in": ["desk"]}], "period": {"preset": "last_30_days"}, "compare": "previous_period"}
- "Which team books the most rooms?" -> {"measure": "reservations", "breakdown": ["team"], "filters": [{"dimension": "resource_type", "in": ["meeting_room"]}], "period": {"preset": "last_90_days"}}
- "Requests by category in Lisbon this year" -> {"measure": "requests", "breakdown": ["category"], "filters": [{"dimension": "office", "in": ["<lisbon office id>"]}], "period": {"preset": "year_to_date"}}

Returns a list of resources available to make a reservation at the given start and end times for the given users.
- If user requests a specific resource name, use this tool to find it because not all resources are returned by default.
- Resources are returned in the order of priority, the ones with the highest priority are returned first, use them first.
- This tool will return permission errors if the user does not have permission to create the requested reservation.
- To only find resources on a floor or in a zone the user names, pass floor_id or zone_id from list_office_places.
- Only the top 5 resources are returned; total says how many are available in all. Use total for "how many desks are free" questions. To list every available resource (with its floor), e.g. for a full list or a CSV, pass all: true.

Example responses:
- Example 1, available desk and room, prefer the desk:
	- {"resources":[{"id": "reso_cafb552b-e49a-4035-b7d9-518875e3d342", "name": "Desk 1", "type": "desk"},{"id": "reso_fbaaaf6b-6d03-4a20-b585-580970abeb41", "name": "Meeting Room 2", "type": "meeting_room"}],"total":2}
- Example 2, available room and desk, prefer the room:
	- {"resources":[{"id": "reso_7d38458b-c1dc-4b47-aa14-51d2050508c5", "name": "Meeting Room 1", "type": "meeting_room"},{"id": "reso_6ae6d00b-ab65-49b5-9478-21481fd92a73", "name": "Desk 2", "type": "desk"}]}
- Example 3, two available rooms, only one has an online meeting provider available:
	- {"resources":[{"id": "reso_7d38458b-c1dc-4b47-aa14-51d2050508c5", "name": "Meeting Room 1", "type": "meeting_room", "online_meeting_provider": "teams_for_business"},{"id": "reso_6ae6d00b-ab65-49b5-9478-21481fd92a73", "name": "Meeting Room 2", "type": "meeting_room"}]}
- Example 4, all: true, every available desk with its floor:
	- {"resources":[{"id": "reso_cafb552b-e49a-4035-b7d9-518875e3d342", "name": "Desk 1", "type": "desk", "floor": "Floor 2"},{"id": "reso_6ae6d00b-ab65-49b5-9478-21481fd92a73", "name": "Desk 2", "type": "desk", "floor": "Floor 2"}],"total":2}
- When no available resources are found, the response is an empty list: {"resources":[],"total":0}

Example responses for permission errors:
- Example 1, user cannot create reservations on behalf of others, only for himself:
  - {"permission_error":"user does not have permission to create reservations for others"}
- Example 2, user cannot create reservations in the past:
  - {"permission_error":"user is not allowed to create reservations in the past"}
- Example 3, office does not allow creating recurring reservations for resources of type desk:
  - {"permission_error":"office does not allow creating recurring reservations for resources of type desk"}
- Example 4, user cannot create reservations for the requested users:
  - {"permission_error":"user does not have permission to create reservations for the requested users"}

